$ ah --help
AIHelper CLI toolbox for AI agents and developers

Usage: ah [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  ai       AI-agent manual and agent integration
  mcp      Model Context Protocol server
  plugins  Plugin management commands
  secrets  Encrypted secret vault management
  upgrade  Check for and install trusted AIHelper releases
  ctx      Context-reduction utilities
  file     File utilities
  git      Git-focused utilities
  http     HTTP workflow utilities
  project  Project detection utilities
  run      Command execution check utilities
  search   Search utilities
  task     Task recipe utilities
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json        Return machine-readable JSON output
      --quiet       Suppress command output
      --cwd <PATH>  Set working directory
      --limit <N>   Cap output lines/items when supported
  -h, --help        Print help
  -V, --version     Print version

$ ah ai --help
AI-agent manual and agent integration

Usage: ai [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  info       Show full AI-agent manual for available commands
  install    Register the AIHelper MCP server and rules block in an AI agent
  uninstall  Remove the AIHelper MCP server and rules block from an AI agent
  status     Report AIHelper integration state for known AI agents
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json        Return machine-readable JSON output
      --quiet       Suppress command output
      --cwd <PATH>  Set working directory
      --limit <N>   Cap output lines/items when supported
  -h, --help        Print help

$ ah ai help --help
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Usage: help [COMMAND]...

Arguments:
  [COMMAND]...  Print help for the subcommand(s)

$ ah ai info --help
Show full AI-agent manual for available commands

Usage: info [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --domain <DOMAIN>  Show manual only for a single command domain
      --json             Return machine-readable JSON output
      --quiet            Suppress command output
      --cwd <PATH>       Set working directory
      --limit <N>        Cap output lines/items when supported
  -h, --help             Print help

$ ah ai install --help
Register the AIHelper MCP server and rules block in an AI agent

Usage: install [OPTIONS] <TARGET>

Arguments:
  <TARGET>  Agent target, for example claude or codex

Options:
      --json                   Return machine-readable JSON output
      --scope <SCOPE>          Configuration scope understood by the target agent [possible values: local, project, user]
      --quiet                  Suppress command output
      --transport <TRANSPORT>  MCP transport written into the agent configuration;                              `managed` uses the Windows managed service endpoint [default: stdio] [possible values: stdio, http, managed]
      --cwd <PATH>             Set working directory
      --url <URL>              Loopback MCP endpoint; only valid with --transport http
      --limit <N>              Cap output lines/items when supported
      --mcp-only               Register the MCP server without touching the rules file
      --rules-only             Install the rules block without registering the MCP server
  -y, --yes                    Skip the interactive confirmation prompt
      --dry-run                Report planned commands and file changes without performing them
  -h, --help                   Print help

